WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.907
The applied challenge returns the two longest completed stays per department.

00:00:03.907 --> 00:00:08.222
The CTE calculates stay days and assigns ROW_NUMBER within each department.

00:00:08.222 --> 00:00:11.122
Stay duration descending defines the main order.

00:00:11.122 --> 00:00:14.247
Admission ID breaks exact duration ties.

00:00:14.247 --> 00:00:17.147
The outer query keeps row numbers one and two.

00:00:17.147 --> 00:00:20.932
After running it, explain why admission-level detail is preserved.

00:00:20.932 --> 00:00:26.027
Connect this idea to an operations team comparing each event with the previous and next event.

00:00:26.027 --> 00:00:30.882
Ask what could go wrong if the concept were misunderstood: could rows be duplicated,

00:00:30.882 --> 00:00:37.537
important records disappear, categories be interpreted incorrectly, or a report become difficult to reproduce?

00:00:37.537 --> 00:00:42.582
A strong analyst can explain both the SQL operation and the assumption behind it.

00:00:42.582 --> 00:00:47.680
After the example, summarize the idea in one plain-language sentence before moving on.
